chrome://downloads fits a phone's width.

The download card is clamp(550px, 80%, 680px) wide, and the list keeps that
plus its margins as a minimum, so on a 377px phone the page scrolled
sideways and each item's copy-link, show-in-folder and remove buttons sat
off screen. Below 598px the card fills the window instead, with narrower
margins.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-downloads-narrow.patch

diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/item.css b/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/item.css
index 71ae0c1..95836fa 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/item.css
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/item.css
@@ -172,6 +172,17 @@ cr-button {
   margin: 18px 24px;
 }
 
+/* See manager.css: on a phone every pixel of the card goes to the name. */
+@media (max-width: 597px) {
+  .icon-wrapper {
+    margin: 18px 12px;
+  }
+
+  #details {
+    padding-inline-start: 0;
+  }
+}
+
 .icon,
 #file-icon-wrapper {
   height: 32px;
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/manager.css b/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/manager.css
index 5d92f27..5738a7b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/manager.css
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/downloads/manager.css
@@ -44,6 +44,18 @@ cr-toast-manager {
   --cr-toast-max-width: var(--downloads-card-width);
 }
 
+/* A window narrower than the card's 550px floor plus its margins -- a phone.
+ * The card fills the window instead, so its copy, show-in-folder and remove
+ * buttons are on screen rather than past its right edge. */
+@media (max-width: 597px) {
+  downloads-item,
+  #downloadsList,
+  cr-toast-manager {
+    --downloads-card-margin: 12px;
+    --downloads-card-width: calc(100% - 2 * var(--downloads-card-margin));
+  }
+}
+
 #downloadsList {
   min-width: calc(
     var(--downloads-card-width) + 2 * var(--downloads-card-margin));
